CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\[main\.assigns\.\d+\] .* Check that x is assignable: FAILURE$
--
Checks that a variable declared before a loop, only used in the loop, and
overwritten before it is read in each iteration (i.e., dead at the loop head)
is a loop local: it need not be in the loop assigns clause. Front-ends such
as Kani declare all temporaries at the start of a function.
